    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41979" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rŭgĭo</span></b> ,
		īre, v. n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to roar</i>, as a lion,
					<i><span class="en">Spart. Get. 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Psa.
				21, 13</span></i>; Auct. Carm. Philom. 49; <i>to
			bray</i>, as an ass, <i><span class="en">Amm. 27, 3, 1</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">onager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Job, 6, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quasi ursi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Isa. 59, 11</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>to rumble</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rugientem saturare ventrem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. 52, 2, § 6</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>To call aloud</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Psa.
				37, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Jer. 25, 30</span></i>.</div>
